<h2><svg class="neon-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="17" y2="17"></line></svg> Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Do I need programming skills to use TestFit?</div><div class="faq-answer">Not for basic use. The marketplace configurators can be used without any coding. However, creating custom functions or advanced workflows benefits from programming knowledge, particularly C# or Python.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I monetize configurators I create?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, TestFit allows developers to publish paid configurators to the marketplace. You set your own pricing and earn revenue when other users purchase your tools.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How does TestFit compare to Grasshopper?</div><div class="faq-answer">TestFit is cloud-based and more accessible for sharing tools, while Grasshopper is local and requires Rhino. TestFit focuses on reusable building blocks and API access, while Grasshopper offers more flexibility for one-off parametric scripts.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I export to Revit or other BIM software?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, TestFit supports export to Revit (RVT), IFC, DWG, and other common formats. The quality of the export depends on the complexity of your model and which configurators you used.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Is there a limit to model complexity on the free tier?</div><div class="faq-answer">The free tier has compute limits rather than model complexity limits. Simple models process quickly, while complex calculations may require a Professional account for adequate computational resources.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I use TestFit offline?</div><div class="faq-answer">No, TestFit is a fully cloud-based platform and requires an internet connection. All geometry processing happens on TestFit's servers, which is what enables the powerful computational capabilities.</div></div>
